# DBUG1 (stream S1-crt) - Win32 calls whose decomp declaration has another arity than the real API; the x86 code
# only worked because the missing argument was already on the stack (docs/PATCHES.md "DBUG1").

@@ DBUG1 src/staging/blk_00b00000_od.cpp 0x00b01510
# x86 0x00b01510 (/Od, thiscall, ret 4): `lea eax,[ebp-0x148]; push eax` (the 0x140-byte local), the virtual call
# through slot 6 (vtable +0x18), `push eax` (its result), `call [FindFirstFileA]`. The IAT slot 0x00fdf070 is
# kernel32 FindFirstFileA(LPCSTR, LPWIN32_FIND_DATAA) (stdcall, 8 bytes; the unit's other declaration binds the
# same slot with both parameters): the local is the second argument, left on the stack by a slot-6 callee that
# takes no stack argument (BSFile's GetFileName, slot 6 without parameters in bsfile_console.cpp 0x00b003c0, whose
# body is FindFirstFileA(GetFileName(), &findData)). The decomp declares the slot with that push as a parameter and
# FindFirstFileA with one, so on the target the find data pointer was never passed. Fix: slot 6 without parameters
# and the call through a two-parameter pointer to the import (the unit's own idiom at 0x00b01af0); MSVC pushes
# the local, calls slot 6 and pushes its result, the same code.
<<<
    virtual int vfn_6(char* data);
===
    virtual int vfn_6();
>>>
<<<
FindFirstFileA((const char*)vfn_6(data))
===
((int(__stdcall*)(const char*, void*))&FindFirstFileA)((const char*)vfn_6(), data)
>>>
